# suno-dl session cookie — copy to .env and paste your value below.
#
# How to extract:
#   1. Open https://suno.com in your browser and log in.
#   2. Open DevTools (macOS: Cmd+Opt+I, Linux: F12).
#   3. Go to Application → Cookies → https://suno.com
#   4. Find the cookie named `__session` and copy its `Value` column.
#   5. Paste it as the value below (no quotes needed).
#
# Then export it in your shell:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# Notes:
# - .env is gitignored. Never commit a real cookie value.
# - The cookie typically lasts a few days; re-extract when it expires.
# - suno-dl reads SUNO_SESSION_COOKIE from the environment only — never
#   from disk — so you can also just `export SUNO_SESSION_COOKIE=...`
#   directly in your shell without using this file.

SUNO_SESSION_COOKIE=paste_your___session_cookie_value_here
